    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2025-10-17",
        "action_desc": "Introduced in House",
        "text": "<p><strong>Head Start Shutdown Protection Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill requires the Department of Health and Human Services to reimburse a state, local government, or school district that uses its funds to maintain participation in the Head Start program or the Early Head Start program during a government shutdown in which there is a lapse in federal appropriations for the programs.</p><p>The Head Start programs provide comprehensive early childhood education and development services to low-income children. The programs seek to promote school readiness through the provision of educational, health, nutritional, social, and other services.&nbsp;</p>",
        "update_date": "2025-10-23T13:52:22Z"
      }
    ]
  },
